      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T21:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that `le32toh` does not change anything for APs that are little endian (which is most/all AP we work with for ChromeOS). I add the phrase `(no-op for most systems)` to call that information out.\n\nSince this validation function promises to return the data in host endianess, it seems appropriate to have this conversion here. I will admit that the assumption that the host is little endian is littered through this code, so we could remove this conversion. I like having it for completeness sake though.\n\nThis code does work as written, and I have verified it via testing. The V1 version serializes data in little endian which is a departure from how we normally encode TPMV data. Since both GSC and AP are little endian (in most cases), there does not need to be any conversion for V1 (which is why it is a no-op).",
      "parentUuid": "ec7b9fae_b3e0ca19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2575,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 2575,
        "endChar": 11
